[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Definition lists
[/meta]

h1. Definition Lists

Tests for Section 15 of the specification.

h2. Short form

h3. Terms and definitions {#definitions-basic}
[code om]
; Term
: Definition text
; Another term
: Another definition
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>Definition text</dd>
  <dt>Another term</dt>
  <dd>Another definition</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Several terms and several definitions {#definitions-multiple}
[code om]
; JPEG
; JPG
: A lossy image format for photographs.
: Pronounced "jay-peg".
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>JPEG</dt>
  <dt>JPG</dt>
  <dd>A lossy image format for photographs.</dd>
  <dd>Pronounced "jay-peg".</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Colons belong to the term {#definitions-colon-in-term}
[code om]
; Note: deprecated
: Use the new API instead.
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Note: deprecated</dt>
  <dd>Use the new API instead.</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. There is no one-line form {#definitions-no-one-line-form}
[code om]
; Term : not a definition
: The real definition
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Term : not a definition</dt>
  <dd>The real definition</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Inline formatting in terms and definitions {#definitions-formatting}
[code om]
; *Bold* term
: Definition with `code` and _emphasis_
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt><strong>Bold</strong> term</dt>
  <dd>Definition with <code>code</code> and <em>emphasis</em></dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. A term ends a paragraph without a blank line {#definitions-interrupt-paragraph}
[code om]
Glossary:
; Term
: Definition
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Glossary:</p>
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>Definition</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Indentation is ignored {#definitions-indented}
[code om]
  ; Term
  : Definition
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>Definition</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h2. Space after the marker

h3. Smiley at line start is text {#definitions-no-space-smiley}
[code om]
:)
[/code]
[code html]
<p>:)</p>
[/code]

h3. Semicolon without a space is text {#definitions-no-space-term}
[code om]
;not a term
[/code]
[code html]
<p>;not a term</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped term marker is text {#definitions-escaped-term}
[code om]
\; not a term
[/code]
[code html]
<p>; not a term</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped definition marker is text {#definitions-escaped-definition}
[code om]
\: not a definition
[/code]
[code html]
<p>: not a definition</p>
[/code]

h2. Continuation lines

h3. Unmarked line continues the definition {#definitions-continuation}
[code om]
; Address
: 12 Main Street
Springfield
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Address</dt>
  <dd>12 Main Street<br>
  Springfield</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Unmarked line after a term is an error {#definitions-continuation-after-term}
[code om]
; Term
Not a definition
[/code]
[code error]
term-without-definition 1
[/code]

h2. Errors

h3. Definition with no term {#definitions-error-no-term}
[code om]
: Orphan definition
[/code]
[code error]
definition-without-term 1
[/code]

h3. Definition after a paragraph and a blank line {#definitions-error-after-paragraph}
[code om]
Some text.

: Orphan definition
[/code]
[code error]
definition-without-term 3
[/code]

h3. Definition after a blank line ends the previous list {#definitions-error-after-blank}
[code om]
; Term
: Definition

: Orphan definition
[/code]
[code error]
definition-without-term 4
[/code]

h3. Term followed by a blank line {#definitions-error-term-blank}
[code om]
; Term

: Definition
[/code]
[code error]
term-without-definition 1
[/code]

h3. Term at the end of the document {#definitions-error-term-at-end}
[code om]
; Term
[/code]
[code error]
term-without-definition 1
[/code]

h3. Term followed by a heading {#definitions-error-term-heading}
[code om]
; Term
h2. Heading
[/code]
[code error]
term-without-definition 1
[/code]

h3. Second of two terms followed by nothing {#definitions-error-second-term}
[code om]
; First
: Defined
; Second
[/code]
[code error]
term-without-definition 3
[/code]

h2. Long form

h3. Single paragraph {#definitions-long-basic}
[code om]
[def Term]
A longer definition that
spans multiple lines.
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>A longer definition that<br>
    spans multiple lines.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Several paragraphs {#definitions-long-paragraphs}
[code om]
[def Term]
First paragraph.

Second paragraph.
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>First paragraph.</p>
    <p>Second paragraph.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Code inside a long definition {#definitions-long-code}
[code om]
[def build]
Run this:

```
om build
```
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>build</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>Run this:</p>
    <pre><code>om build
</code></pre>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Formatted term {#definitions-long-formatted-term}
[code om]
[def *Bold* term]
Text.
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt><strong>Bold</strong> term</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>Text.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. List inside a long definition {#definitions-long-list}
[code om]
[def Steps]
# Open the file
# Save it
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Steps</dt>
  <dd>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the file</li>
      <li>Save it</li>
    </ol>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Paragraph followed by a list inside a long definition {#definitions-long-paragraph-list}
[code om]
[def Colors]
Primary colors:
* Red
* Blue
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Colors</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>Primary colors:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Red</li>
      <li>Blue</li>
    </ul>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Long form without a term is an error {#definitions-long-no-term}
[code om]
[def]
Text.
[/def]
[/code]
[code error]
def-without-term 1
[/code]

h3. Headings are not allowed inside {#definitions-long-no-heading}
[code om]
[def Term]
h2. Heading
[/def]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h3. Long definitions do not nest {#definitions-long-no-nesting}
[code om]
[def Outer]
[def Inner]
Text.
[/def]
[/def]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h3. Short form is not allowed inside {#definitions-long-no-short-form}
[code om]
[def Outer]
; Inner
: Text
[/def]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h3. Unclosed long definition {#definitions-long-unclosed}
[code om]
[def Term]
Text.
[/code]
[code error]
unclosed-block 1
[/code]

h2. Grouping

h3. Blank line separates lists {#definitions-grouping-blank-line}
[code om]
; Apple
: A fruit
; Banana
: Another fruit

; Orange
: Yet another fruit
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Apple</dt>
  <dd>A fruit</dd>
  <dt>Banana</dt>
  <dd>Another fruit</dd>
</dl>
<dl>
  <dt>Orange</dt>
  <dd>Yet another fruit</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Short form followed by long form {#definitions-grouping-short-long}
[code om]
; Apple
: A fruit
[def Banana]
Another fruit.
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Apple</dt>
  <dd>A fruit</dd>
  <dt>Banana</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>Another fruit.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Long form followed by short form {#definitions-grouping-long-short}
[code om]
[def Apple]
A fruit.
[/def]
; Banana
: Another fruit
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Apple</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>A fruit.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt>Banana</dt>
  <dd>Another fruit</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Consecutive long forms {#definitions-grouping-long-long}
[code om]
[def Apple]
A fruit.
[/def]
[def Banana]
Another fruit.
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Apple</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>A fruit.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt>Banana</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>Another fruit.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Long forms separated by a blank line {#definitions-grouping-long-blank}
[code om]
[def Apple]
A fruit.
[/def]

[def Banana]
Another fruit.
[/def]
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Apple</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>A fruit.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
<dl>
  <dt>Banana</dt>
  <dd>
    <p>Another fruit.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h2. Profiles

h3. Definition lists are not allowed in the basic profile {#definitions-profile-basic}
; profile
: basic
[code om]
; Term
: Definition
[/code]
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 1
[/code]

h3. Definition lists are allowed in the standard profile {#definitions-profile-standard}
; profile
: standard
[code om]
; Term
: Definition
[/code]
[code html]
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>Definition</dd>
</dl>
[/code]
